<Base title="About Brewster Smyers"><section class="about-layout wrap"><figure><img src={url('images/portrait.webp')} alt="Brewster Smyers in a suit outdoors" width="900" height="1100"/><figcaption>Brewster Smyers · Marblehead, Massachusetts</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">A little about me</p><h1>Most ideas start<br/>with <span>“what if?”</span></h1><p class="lead">I’m Brewster, a junior studying mechanical engineering at Bucknell University, with minors in Mathematics and Business Analytics.</p><div class="prose"><p>I like the point where an idea becomes something tangible. That might mean building a chair at full scale, developing aircraft geometry in SolidWorks, or using a mathematical model to understand how an underwater vehicle floats.</p><p>My interests span automotive engineering, aerospace, robotics, manufacturing and product development. I’m learning to connect design decisions with calculations, practical constraints and the evidence needed to know whether a design works.</p><p>Outside engineering, I ski, cycle and hike. I’ve also worked behind a bar, helped organize fraternity events and supported students through LEAP for Education. Those experiences have taught me to stay organized, communicate clearly and take responsibility for the work in front of me.</p><p>I’m looking for a Summer 2027 internship where I can contribute, learn from experienced engineers and spend time close to the design and build process.</p></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={url('resume/')}>View my resume <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={url('contact/')}>Let’s talk ↗</a></div></div></section></Base>
